ac@acamille.hpl.hp.com (Albert Camilleri) writes:
^L
>OK, so I have been on the quest (thanks due to those who replied), killed
>the Dark One (I think), and am now in possession of the Bell of Opening
>and the Eye of the Aethiopica.

>Q1. Is the Bell one of the 3 items I need to do this rite I keep hearing about?

Yes.

>    If so, I still need the candellabrum and the book. Do I need to go on
>    further quests to get these? Or can I just find them in the dungeon?

Yes, you need the candelabrum and the book. No further quests but the ones
to Vlad and the Wizard to obtain the candelabrum and the book. Then you'll
be ready to use them and go to the Sanctum (you have the candles, don't you?).

>Q2. Should I return the Eye to the Wizard of Balance as charged, or should I
>    keep it for myself? What happens if I put it on?

You are asked to take it to your quest master in the beginning of the quest,
but he will let you keep it. You just have to go back to meet the Wizard of
Balance and then you can return to the normal dungeon with the Eye.
